# 17. INVOICE MANAGEMENT

Both Admin and Salesperson must be able to create invoices.

Admin can create invoices for any authorized client or event and can review and manage all invoices.

Salesperson can create invoices for their own authorized sales and events.

### Invoice creation

Allow users to:

* Select an existing client.
* Create a new client if permitted.
* Link the invoice to an existing event.
* Create an invoice during direct-sale creation.
* Add or edit line items.
* Add discounts.
* Configure advance-payment requirements.
* Record payment information.
* Preview the invoice.
* Save a draft.
* Issue the invoice.
* Download or print a PDF.

### Invoice fields

* Unique invoice number.
* Invoice date.
* Client details.
* Event name.
* Event type.
* Banquet.
* Event date and time.
* Line-item description.
* Quantity.
* Unit price.
* Line-item total.
* Discount.
* Final invoice total.
* Advance payment required: Yes/No.
* Advance requested.
* Actual advance received.
* Payment terms.
* Notes.
* Created by.
* Invoice status.

### Calculations

Calculate all monetary totals using reliable decimal-safe arithmetic.

For each line item:

Line Total = Quantity × Unit Price

Subtotal = Sum of Line Totals

Final Total = Subtotal − Discount

Remaining Balance = Final Total − Total Payments Received

Validate:

* No negative quantities.
* No invalid monetary values.
* Discount does not exceed the permitted total.
* Advance requested does not exceed the invoice total.
* Payments cannot exceed the outstanding balance unless an explicit, audited credit/refund workflow supports it.

Display advance requested and advance received as separate fields.

### Invoice status

Support:

* Draft.
* Issued.
* Partially Paid.
* Paid.
* Cancelled.

Do not mark an invoice paid solely because an advance was requested.

### PDF generation

Generate a clean, professional PDF with:

* PerlEvents branding.
* Business contact details configured by Admin.
* Invoice number.
* Invoice date.
* Client information.
* Event information.
* Itemized charges.
* Discount.
* Total.
