* Client.
* Sale.
* Invoice.
* Event.
* Amount.
* Payment date.
* Payment method.
* Reference number, optional.
* Notes.
* Recorded by.
* Creation timestamp.

Payment methods may include:

* Cash.
* UPI.
* Bank transfer.
* Card.
* Other.

Admin must be able to record and review payments.

Authorized Salespersons may record payments according to configured permissions.

Do not integrate a payment gateway unless separately configured.

Recording a payment means the business has recorded receipt; it does not mean the ERP has independently verified the bank transaction.

Update invoice balances and relevant sales reports consistently.

Do not allow unauthorized users to delete or silently alter payment records.

Use reversal or adjustment records for corrections.

